WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:00.640
Speaker 1: Foreign.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.560
Speaker 1: Hi, my name is Pastor Joshua Kesena.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.440
Speaker 1: So in this video we're going to be talking about how to evangelize.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.050
Speaker 1: How can you evangelize and evangelize effectively?

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.210
Speaker 1: To begin this topic, I would like to share a story about Penn Gillette.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:44.330
Speaker 1: Now, Penn Gillette is a performing magician and he told a story about a particular guy who walked up to him after his show and this guy told him, oh, I really enjoyed the show.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:51.370
Speaker 1: And this part, and this part really stood out to me and was really an enjoyable experience, but I'd like to share something with you.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:59.870
Speaker 1: And he pulled out a book from his pocket and told him, this is a Bible and it's something I believe in strongly and I know it will bless you because Jesus died for you.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:04.190
Speaker 1: And I wrote something at the first page and I'd like to share it with you now.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:12.830
Speaker 1: Penn, being a self professed atheist, a popular one at that, was felt glad that someone would do that.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.310
Speaker 1: And this is what he had to say about it.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:18.190
Speaker 1: Although he does not believe in God or any God at all.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.250
Speaker 1: This is what you have to say about that experience.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.490
Speaker 1: I'll read it for you.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:26.410
Speaker 1: He said, I've always said I don't respect people who don't proselytize.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:32.810
Speaker 1: Now, proselytize means sharing your faith with someone in the hopes of changing their mind so that they can believe what you believe.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.850
Speaker 1: He says, I don't have respect for people who don't proselytize.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.770
Speaker 1: I don't respect that at all.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:54.350
Speaker 1: If you believe there is a heaven and a hell and people could be going to hell or not getting eternal life or whatever, and you think it's not really worth telling them this because it will make it socially awkward.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.590
Speaker 1: I cannot trust someone like that.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:00.910
Speaker 1: How much do you have to hate somebody not to proselytize?

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:09.070
Speaker 1: How much do you have to hate someone to believe there is everlasting life possible for them to get and not tell them that?

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:14.700
Speaker 1: So in a nutshell, he's saying, how much do you have to hate somebody not to share the gospel with them?

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.820
Speaker 1: And it's so true.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.500
Speaker 1: This is why we share the gospel.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:23.340
Speaker 1: Because there is death and there is life in Christ and Christ only should we share the gospel.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:28.620
Speaker 1: So in a few minutes I would like to share with you how to effectively evangelize.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.780
Speaker 1: What is evangelism?

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:34.700
Speaker 1: What is evangelism?

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:41.930
Speaker 1: Evangelism simply means sharing about your faith, sharing and telling someone about Jesus.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.210
Speaker 1: That's what it simply means.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:45.930
Speaker 1: That's what it simply means.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:48.570
Speaker 1: So how do you do this effectively?

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:54.250
Speaker 1: I want to tell you a few key steps on how to evangelize effectively.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.650
Speaker 1: Number one, live like a dead man.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.770
Speaker 1: Now that sounds like a conundrum, because how can a dead man live?

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.570
Speaker 1: To project this point, I'd like to read a particular verse in Galatians 2:20.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.160
Speaker 1: It says, I have been crucified with Christ.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.080
Speaker 1: It is no longer I who live, but Christ who lives in me.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:20.000
Speaker 1: So what this verse is saying in a nutshell, is that you should no longer live for yourself because you have been crucified with Christ.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.079
Speaker 1: You don't live for yourself.

00:03:21.079 --> 00:03:22.480
Speaker 1: Don't leave for your preferences.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.840
Speaker 1: Oh, I don't really like sharing the gospel.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:30.550
Speaker 1: No, you have been crucified with Christ and Christ lives through you, so you ought to share the gospel.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:37.980
Speaker 1: The normal tendency to feel like I want to avoid any socially awkward situation, so I will not share the gospel.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:42.940
Speaker 1: You must die to it because you have died to it in Christ and Christ lives through you.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.940
Speaker 1: Another key step is to use what you have.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.140
Speaker 1: Use your career, use your giftings.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:53.500
Speaker 1: For instance, in the Bible, Luke 10, 25, 37, you can read it when you have the time.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:04:05.070
Speaker 1: Talks about the Samaritan man, the good Samaritan who helped someone using the resources he had, his donkey and his money to ensure the person was well.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:13.150
Speaker 1: So you can use your career, use your platform, use your giftings to share the gospel.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:20.510
Speaker 1: Another key step for evangelism is to preach the gospel intentionally.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:24.840
Speaker 1: Be intentional about preaching the gospel beforehand.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.560
Speaker 1: Know what you want to say and how you want to say it.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:31.320
Speaker 1: Have conversation starters on how you want to evangelize.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.440
Speaker 1: Like Philip to the Ethiopian eunuch in the Book of Acts.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.400
Speaker 1: He asked the.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.280
Speaker 1: He asked the Ethiopian, New York, do you understand what you're reading?

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.280
Speaker 1: Because heard him reading from the book of Isaiah.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:48.040
Speaker 1: And the Ethiopian said, how can I understand unless someone explains to me the Bible says, starting from that, he preached the gospel unto him.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.250
Speaker 1: So here are some few conversation starters for you.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:53.730
Speaker 1: Do you know where people go when they die?

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.250
Speaker 1: Do you think there is more to life than what we see?

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:00.730
Speaker 1: What do you think it takes for someone to go to heaven?

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:06.130
Speaker 1: Now these questions help you set the stage for people to tell you what they believe in already.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.810
Speaker 1: So you can explain the Bible and explain the gospel to them.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:16.750
Speaker 1: You can ask following questions like, okay, why do you think that when they tell you what they believe, how they feel you can get to heaven?

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.310
Speaker 1: You can ask them, why do you think that?

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.030
Speaker 1: You can also ask, what do you mean by that?

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.110
Speaker 1: So that you don't just run off thinking you understand what they are saying.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:25.990
Speaker 1: Meanwhile, you have misunderstood them.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.750
Speaker 1: So ask, what do you mean by that?

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:37.990
Speaker 1: Another conversation starter can be suppose you were to die today and stand before God, and you were to say, why should I let you into my heaven?

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.350
Speaker 1: What would you say?

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:47.380
Speaker 1: And this will help you get an insight into how people think about everlasting life, eternal life and heaven.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:51.620
Speaker 1: So you can thereby correct by sharing what the Gospel really is.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:58.260
Speaker 1: Another key point for evangelism is to rely on the power of the Holy Spirit.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.620
Speaker 1: You are not doing this in your strength and in your strength alone.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:04.340
Speaker 1: You can rely on the power of the Holy Spirit.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:05.740
Speaker 1: Partner with the Holy Spirit.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.230
Speaker 1: Look what the Bible says in Acts chapter one, verse eight.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:14.950
Speaker 1: He says, you shall receive power when the Holy Spirit has come upon you, and we shall witness you shall be witnesses unto me.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:20.550
Speaker 1: So there is a power that comes from the Holy Spirit that enables you to witness the gospel.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.469
Speaker 1: Rely on the power of the Holy Ghost.

00:06:23.469 --> 00:06:27.910
Speaker 1: Decide not to do this by yourself, but with the help of the Holy Spirit.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:37.360
Speaker 1: Just to buttress these points that I've shared, here are a few tools that can enable you when evangelizing.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.360
Speaker 1: Pray for boldness.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:46.520
Speaker 1: Oh my Lord, this is so important because there is a fear that comes with wanting to share the gospel with someone else.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.520
Speaker 1: What if they say no?

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:48.960
Speaker 1: What if they make a sin?

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.240
Speaker 1: What if they get angry?

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.680
Speaker 1: What if they reject me?

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.440
Speaker 1: Pray for boldness.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:07:01.990
Speaker 1: The Bible talks about how the disciples, the apostles, preached the gospel and they were arrested and fled, flogged and warned not to preach the gospel again.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:07.030
Speaker 1: Look at their Response in Acts 4:29 31.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:16.630
Speaker 1: They said, Now, Lord, look to their threats and grant your servants that with all boldness they may speak your word.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:22.150
Speaker 1: They were asking for boldness that with all boldness they may speak your word by stretching out your hand to heal.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:25.990
Speaker 1: And signs and wonders may be done through the name of your holy servant, Jesus.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:29.910
Speaker 1: Now look at what the Bible says happened after they prayed that prayer.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:38.550
Speaker 1: The Bible says, and when they had prayed, the place where they were assembled together was shaken and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit.

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:41.670
Speaker 1: And they spoke the word of God with boldness.

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:44.630
Speaker 1: So there is a boldness that comes from praying.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.150
Speaker 1: Use this tool.

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:48.070
Speaker 1: Use this tool to evangelize.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:51.830
Speaker 1: Another tool is to master the Gospel message well enough.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.880
Speaker 1: Master the gospel message.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.040
Speaker 1: What does salvation mean?

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:56.720
Speaker 1: Learn how to explain it.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:05.200
Speaker 1: There's a tactic that says if you cannot explain something difficult to a 3, 4, 5 year old, you've not learned to master it well Enough.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.440
Speaker 1: So learn the gospel well enough.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:08.800
Speaker 1: What does salvation mean?

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.480
Speaker 1: What does repentance mean?

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.800
Speaker 1: What does it mean to have a new life in Christ?

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:17.360
Speaker 1: Know how to explain these things so that you can answer people's questions on the go.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.330
Speaker 1: I Another tool is to use technology.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:22.010
Speaker 1: Use technology.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:31.690
Speaker 1: We live in a world that is technology based and people have attention spans that are focused on social media.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:33.130
Speaker 1: So use social media.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.250
Speaker 1: Use blogs, use YouTube to explain the gospel.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:40.809
Speaker 1: And it's very important that you understand people don't have time to watch a video.

00:08:41.049 --> 00:08:45.690
Speaker 1: People don't have time to read that tweet if it's not engaging enough at the first time.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:49.810
Speaker 1: So employ storytelling tactics that will keep people's attention.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:55.810
Speaker 1: When you use social media, another tool is to be always ready.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.730
Speaker 1: Always be ready.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:07.250
Speaker 1: The Bible in 1 Peter 3:15 says, Always be ready to give a defense to everyone who asks you a reason for the hope that is in you.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.170
Speaker 1: So always be ready.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.810
Speaker 1: What this looks like is preparing ahead.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:24.130
Speaker 1: I think it's Ravi Zacharias of blessed memory that said he has over 1,000 or 2,000 questions that he knows people will ask about the gospel and he prepares ahead of hand to give them answers.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.050
Speaker 1: So he's always ready.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.290
Speaker 1: So always be ready.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.570
Speaker 1: Always have a short form of the gospel.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:37.410
Speaker 1: For instance, you're in a bus and you only have a limited time frame to share the gospel.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:40.540
Speaker 1: Have a short version or instead also.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:41.700
Speaker 1: Not instead also.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:47.020
Speaker 1: If you have longer time to share somebody, you have a longer time to share with that colleague or that friend.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.020
Speaker 1: Have a longer version that you can tell people.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:52.300
Speaker 1: Also, use your stories how you came to the faith.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.060
Speaker 1: Use your personal stories.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:10:00.380
Speaker 1: People love and can relate to stories that have more personality to it.

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:04.000
Speaker 1: So you can use your personal stories to share the gospel in.

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:07.630
Speaker 1: In conclusion, you ought to live like a dead man.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:08.750
Speaker 1: Christ died for you.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:12.510
Speaker 1: You died with Christ on the cross and now you live the life you live.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.150
Speaker 1: Is Christ living through you?

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:16.390
Speaker 1: So live like a dead man and share the gospel.

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:19.510
Speaker 1: Overcome that fear of being rejected.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:23.270
Speaker 1: Overcome that fear of having socially awkward scenarios.

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.390
Speaker 1: Also use what you have.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:29.430
Speaker 1: Use your platform, use your giftings, use your career.

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:32.090
Speaker 1: Use your social media to share the gospel.

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:36.090
Speaker 1: Another thing is to preach the gospel intentionally.

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:42.890
Speaker 1: Prepare ahead of hand and then lastly, but not the least, rely on the power of the Holy Spirit.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:53.530
Speaker 1: To round this up, I'd like to tell a story about a particular preacher who was talking and he said he was driving home on a foggy evening on a road, and this road was hilly.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:59.580
Speaker 1: So what that meant was there were a lot of curves that somebody at the other curve would not see what is coming from the last.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:10:59.940
Speaker 1: From.

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:00.940
Speaker 1: From the other side.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.340
Speaker 1: So blind spots on the road.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:07.660
Speaker 1: So the person in front of him had an accident, a ghastly accident.

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:15.660
Speaker 1: So he was able to back his car up out of the curve for people who are coming and align it horizontally so people can see and stop.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.740
Speaker 1: And he ran to the other side of the curve.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:21.660
Speaker 1: And when people are coming, because it was foggy, he could not stand ahead of time.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.860
Speaker 1: So he would stand and jump out almost at the last minute.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:29.430
Speaker 1: So people have to screech and stop and halt so that they don't have an accident.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.710
Speaker 1: Now these people were insulting him.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:32.790
Speaker 1: Why are you doing this?

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:34.630
Speaker 1: I could have hit you.

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:35.550
Speaker 1: Why are you doing this?

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:42.230
Speaker 1: And they kept insulting him until they went around the curve and saw what he saved them from.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:44.150
Speaker 1: It's the same thing we are talking about.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:48.030
Speaker 1: There is eternal life in Christ if you share the gospel.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:54.540
Speaker 1: If you refuse to share the gospel, what you are doing is talking to that man, not jumping in front of cars because, oh, what will people say?

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:55.580
Speaker 1: They will insult me.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:00.140
Speaker 1: They will say I'm being foolish and they will drive off.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:04.540
Speaker 1: But we share the gospel because there is death and there is eternal life.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.820
Speaker 1: And eternal life is found in Christ and Christ alone.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:14.060
Speaker 1: So I hope you will be able to learn one or two things on how to share the gospel effectively.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:22.150
Speaker 1: It.
